Running the Scripts

PowerShell scripts need an elevated session. Get-MpComputerStatus returns incomplete data without it, the Security log is unreadable without it, and performance counters need it.

powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
.\Invoke-SystemHealthCheck.ps1
.\Get-LocalUserReport.ps1 -OutputPath C:\Audit\users.csv
.\Get-EventLogReport.ps1 -Hours 24

Bash scripts run as a normal user but report more as root:

bash
chmod +x *.sh
./sysinfo.sh
./ollama-check.sh -o /tmp/ollama-report.txt
sudo ./user-audit.sh -o audit.csv

Every script takes -h for its options.
